Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: satellite
Upstream-Contact: Terran Satellite <terransatellite@gmail.com>
Comment: The Expat text below is a transcription of the LICENSE file at the
 top of the upstream source tree, reformatted for this file's syntax and not
 reworded. LICENSE is what `make install` puts in
 /usr/share/doc/satellite/copyright, and dh_installdocs puts this file at the
 same path in the package, so the two routes must state the same terms; check
 them against each other whenever either moves.
 .
 The two routes do NOT agree about pcg-cpp-0.98, and that is a known gap rather
 than an oversight: this file carries its Apache-2.0 stanza and the top-level
 LICENSE does not mention it, so a tarball install states only the Expat terms.
 The .deb is correct; `make install` is the route that needs deciding.

Files: *
Copyright: 2026 Terran Satellite <terransatellite@gmail.com>
License: Expat

Files: pcg-cpp-0.98/*
Copyright: 2014 Melissa O'Neill <oneill@pcg-random.org>
License: Apache-2.0
Comment: The PCG random number generators, vendored into the source tree and
 header-only, used by random.cpp for satellite.random (DESIGN.md section 18).
 The stanza is here because `Files: *` above would otherwise state the wrong
 licence and the wrong copyright holder for this directory. This is the ONLY
 part of the tree that is not the upstream author's own work.
 .
 Version 0.98 is licensed under Apache-2.0 alone. Later releases of pcg-cpp
 offer a choice of Apache-2.0 or Expat; this one does not, so do not restate it
 as dual-licensed on the strength of the project's later terms.

